From dd181669bc24fb578b8aa4548b2f0120dab13870 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sergej19882906 <sergej19882906@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:59:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luci: add Argon theme v3.1.4 as the default LuCI theme

Vendor the Argon theme (jerrykuku/luci-theme-argon v3.1.4) into the tree as
package/luci-theme-argon. The upstream project ships a single Makefile at
the repository root, which the OpenWrt feed scanner does not pick up
(scripts/metadata.pm requires a directory component before 'Makefile'),
and luci.mk needs htdocs/, po/, root/ and ucode/ to be present in the
package directory at parse time. Vendoring the sources is therefore the
only way to get both the theme and its translations into the image.

The theme is registered in the LuCI theme list and selected by default
through the new uci-defaults script 35-pejir-theme-argon. A new name is
required because uci-defaults scripts run once and are removed afterwards:
the already executed 30-luci-theme and 30_luci-theme-cyberpunk scripts
would never run again on an upgraded device.

Cyberpunk stays in the image and stays selectable in the Design list.
